\import{fdip-macros}
\meta{agent-authored}{true}
\tag{fdip}
\taxon{Proposition}
\title{The Hilbert space generated by coarse histories}
\date{2026-11-09}

\p{For the cylinder vectors constructed in \ref{fdip-00HN}, let}

##{\mathcal H_{\mathrm{hist}}=\overline{\operatorname{span}\{v_F:F\text{ a bounded positive-time coarse cylinder}\}}\subseteq\mathcal H.}

\p{The reflection-null space consists of the cylinders #{F} with #{\|v_F\|=0}. The map
#{[F]\mapsto v_F} identifies the completion of the reflection-positive cylinder
quotient with #{\mathcal H_{\mathrm{hist}}}. Positive time translation #{F\mapsto
F_a}, which replaces each #{t_j} by #{t_j+a}, obeys}

##{v_{F_a}=S_av_F,\qquad a\geq0.}

\p{The space #{\mathcal H_{\mathrm{hist}}} is reducing for every #{S_a} and carries
the strongly continuous semigroup #{S_a|_{\mathcal H_{\mathrm{hist}}}}. Moreover,
#{\im J\subseteq\mathcal H_{\mathrm{hist}}}, with
equality exactly when #{\im J} is reducing for all
#{S_a}. In the interacting example of \ref{fdip-00HJ}, this
inclusion is strict.}

\proof{

\p{The inner-product identity of \ref{fdip-00HN} gives an isometry from the cylinder
quotient onto the span of the #{v_F}; completion gives the stated identification.
Shifting all positive times by #{a} puts #{S_a} at the left of the defining string,
proving the translation formula. It preserves the span and, by boundedness, its
closure. Self-adjointness gives reduction as in \ref{fdip-00HI}; restriction
preserves strong continuity.}

\p{Time-zero observables give #{v_{f(x_0)}=Jf} for bounded #{f}. Such #{f} are dense
in #{L^2(\rho)}, so #{\im J\subseteq\mathcal H_{\mathrm{hist}}}.
Equality holds exactly when #{\im J} is invariant under every #{S_t}.
Indeed invariance, together with invariance under all lifted multipliers, keeps every
#{v_F} in that range. Conversely equality makes the range invariant by the preceding
paragraph. Thus \ref{fdip-00HJ} has}

##{\im J\subsetneq\mathcal H_{\mathrm{hist}}.}

}

\p{This history time semigroup acts on this larger space of histories. Its existence
does not turn the compressed family on the one-time space #{L^2(\rho)} into a
semigroup. This distinction uses an explicit finite-volume realization; reflection
positivity in an unrelated model still requires that model's separate time-translation
and continuity hypotheses.}
